[32m+[m[32m### MEMBER-005 — No admin member-management UI (search/byId/setActive/setRole all backend-only)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Severity:** Medium (feature gap, not a misbehaving code path — an admin[m
[32m+[m[32mcould not look up a member, view their detail, deactivate them, or[m
[32m+[m[32mchange their role from anywhere in the app)[m
[32m+[m[32m**Status:** Fixed on branch `admin-members-ui`[m
[32m+[m[32m**Area:** Members / Admin UI[m
[32m+[m[32m**File:** `src/app/admin/members/page.tsx` (new), `src/app/admin/page.tsx`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Original behavior:** all four procedures existed and worked correctly.[m
[32m+[m[32m`search` was only ever called from the member-picker embedded in[m
[32m+[m[32m`admin/companies/[id]/page.tsx` (there to link a member to a company,[m
[32m+[m[32mnot to manage members generally). `byId`, `setActive`, and `setRole` had[m
[32m+[m[32mzero callers anywhere under `src/app/**` — confirmed by grepping for[m
[32m+[m[32m`members.byId`, `members.setActive`, `members.setRole` across the[m
[32m+[m[32mfrontend. An admin could not look up a member, view their membership[m
[32m+[m[32mhistory, deactivate an account, or change a role from anywhere in the[m
[32m+[m[32mrunning app.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Fix:** added `/admin/members`, a new admin-only page: a search bar[m
[32m+[m[32mcalling the *unmodified* `members.search`, a result list, and a detail[m
[32m+[m[32mpanel (`members.byId`) for the selected member showing membership[m
[32m+[m[32mhistory plus activate/deactivate and role-change controls wired to the[m
[32m+[m[32m*unmodified* `members.setActive`/`setRole`. None of the four procedures'[m
[32m+[m[32minput schemas, output shapes, or error codes changed. Linked from a new[m
[32m+[m[32m"Members" button on `/admin`'s existing button row, alongside[m
[32m+[m[32mCompanies/Reports/Announcements (same pattern — reachable only from the[m
[32m+[m[32madmin dashboard, not from `NavBar`).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**MEMBER-003 handled explicitly, not silently:** `setActive`/`setRole`[m
[32m+[m[32mreturn `undefined` instead of throwing on a bad id. Verified directly[m
[32m+[m[32magainst the running dev server that this is still true (id `99999`[m
[32m+[m[32mreturns `null`/`undefined`, no error). The new page's mutation handlers[m
[32m+[m[32mcheck the returned row before treating the change as applied and show an[m
[32m+[m[32minline error if it comes back empty — a defensive check in the new UI[m
[32m+[m[32mcode, not a fix to MEMBER-003 itself, which is untouched.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Not in scope for this fix:** MEMBER-001 (arbitrary-match lookup) and[m
[32m+[m[32mMEMBER-002 (latest-endDate-wins membership resolution) are unrelated[m
[32m+[m[32mprocedures and untouched. `search`'s own behavior (matches any role, not[m
[32m+[m[32mjust "member"; empty query returns everyone up to the default limit) is[m
[32m+[m[32msurfaced as-is — the new page doesn't restrict results to `role:[m
[32m+[m[32m"member"` since the backend doesn't either, and admins reasonably need[m
[32m+[m[32mto find trainers/other admins here too (e.g. to demote one).[m
